Hephaestus — hard sciences and productive work (@hephaestus: 0, is #chapter, #making-and-maintenance "inquiry/Inquiry.lingua#r_75MNKZQKNB0XBG021SWWW2HASB", #making-and-maintenance "engineering/Engineering.lingua#r_5DA6VY09MAD2N8D9SH0FFJVV68", #making-and-maintenance "materials/Materials.lingua#r_14HP6K610XB12E2WGNK9A6VN8D", #making-and-maintenance "utilities/Utilities.lingua#r_23Z5YYXGRA1JDFD4BAM955JMNX", #hephaestus "inquiry/Inquiry.lingua#r_75MNKZQKNB0XBG021SWWW2HASB", #hephaestus "chemistry/Chemistry.lingua#r_2NWJY1HCKPBM4T6YQSDHN8S3S0", #hephaestus "engineering/Engineering.lingua#r_5DA6VY09MAD2N8D9SH0FFJVV68", #hephaestus "physics/Physics.lingua#r_04A5CP8RTBERZEN4XCCDQ3T47W", #part-of "../Ergon.lingua#r_FE78A5A2D2A3261F711703DCC1", #hephaestus "materials/Materials.lingua#r_14HP6K610XB12E2WGNK9A6VN8D", #hephaestus "utilities/Utilities.lingua#r_23Z5YYXGRA1JDFD4BAM955JMNX") { r_00000000000000000000002001
Within Ergon, Hephaestus connects mathematics, hard sciences, engineering, computing, production, and maintenance. Build useful knowledge through reading, observation, practice, and shared work.

Follow materials, energy, equipment, skills, information, and maintenance through the systems that make useful things possible. [Shared inquiry](inquiry/Inquiry.lingua#r_75MNKZQKNB0XBG021SWWW2HASB) and [quantitative and technical literacy](inquiry/quantitative-literacy/Quantitative-literacy.lingua#r_4XVN56PQC13JGNFPV0CSGXDCZ2) supply connected foundations. The quantitative readings develop units, drawings, material balances, usable output, measurement, and an infrastructure account from substantial external books and original studies.

Find original materials through the [Open Textbook Library](https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks), [LibreTexts](https://libretexts.org/), [Appropedia](https://www.appropedia.org/), and [Project Gutenberg](https://www.gutenberg.org/).

Choose a particular work, record its direct download link and attribution, and connect selected passages or practical activities through ordinary Records. These links are starting points for authors.

[Earth — materials, processes, and geological history](../gaia/earth/Earth.lingua#r_5H7Y6QD1FW4Z0JJ6C7SH4DDHXH) begins with [Geology — Earth materials, processes, history, and investigation](../gaia/earth/geology/Geology.lingua#r_3CK43VQS79NK0STWNPSCS8YM06) for the materials, deposits, water pathways, and ground histories underlying extraction and infrastructure. The resource and infrastructure studies connect geological evidence with processing, construction, and maintenance questions.

Follow extraction, processing, and their supporting work through [Engineering — systems, design, construction, and operation](engineering/Engineering.lingua#r_5DA6VY09MAD2N8D9SH0FFJVV68), beginning with [Mining and mineral engineering — extraction, processing, and continuing work](engineering/mining-and-mineral-engineering/Mining-and-mineral-engineering.lingua#r_22HJPS3RTK5EX1J55YJP75PHYA).

Follow feedstocks, useful material properties, production, and recovery through [Resources and materials — feedstocks, useful properties, production, and recovery](materials/Materials.lingua#r_14HP6K610XB12E2WGNK9A6VN8D).

**Water and sanitation:** [Utilities — water, energy and the services that sustain other work](utilities/Utilities.lingua#r_23Z5YYXGRA1JDFD4BAM955JMNX) follows water sources, quality, delivery, treatment, recovery and the work required to maintain service.

Understand models and observations, learn the mathematical tools they use, and connect them with the design, production, and maintenance of useful systems. A question can cross several fields without requiring a reader to complete every subject first.

Begin with [shared inquiry](inquiry/Inquiry.lingua#r_75MNKZQKNB0XBG021SWWW2HASB) and [quantitative and technical literacy](inquiry/quantitative-literacy/Quantitative-literacy.lingua#r_4XVN56PQC13JGNFPV0CSGXDCZ2). Questions about assumptions and evidence return to [Philosophy](../../scholazein/philosophy/Philosophy.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001001).

[Chemistry](chemistry/Chemistry.lingua#r_2NWJY1HCKPBM4T6YQSDHN8S3S0) begins with [General chemistry](chemistry/general-chemistry/General-chemistry.lingua#r_206GS6CVXD8WSY1VX7PRF7136V), from ordinary materials and chemical language through structure, reactions, energy, rates, equilibria, chemical measurement, sustained laboratory study, and independent research.

[Earth — materials, processes, and geological history](../gaia/earth/Earth.lingua#r_5H7Y6QD1FW4Z0JJ6C7SH4DDHXH) connects materials, maps, geological time, tectonics, water, and ground conditions through [Geology — Earth materials, processes, history, and investigation](../gaia/earth/geology/Geology.lingua#r_3CK43VQS79NK0STWNPSCS8YM06), with substantial field, laboratory, numerical, and scholarly study. Its [Nature — Earth, living systems, and their relationships](../gaia/Nature.lingua#r_5DAMNRQZX9M2PRPHVJB673XX21) entrance also connects living systems and their relationships.

Develop charge, fields, matter, induction, waves, radiation and physical evidence through [Physics — fields, matter, motion and physical evidence](physics/Physics.lingua#r_04A5CP8RTBERZEN4XCCDQ3T47W).

**Umbrella:** [Ergon](../Ergon.lingua#r_FE78A5A2D2A3261F711703DCC1). [Hephaestus development register](../../lince/Trails.lingua#r_B6CB9BDC51A6B67584422A89AE) lists every remaining field and subject. Planned material is not a completed reading route. Water and sanitation is a draft; its full treatment and verification remain in progress.
} r_00000000000000000000002001

